From c8f3926a98e77c84536cc253f2b8072cfc87e860 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mavis <Mavis@MiniMax>
Date: Mon, 3 Aug 2026 23:03:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(bpmn): Miro-style color theme for the diagram editor

Replaces bpmn-js's default black-and-white renderer with a color-coded,
rounded, soft-shadowed look that matches the Atlassian design tokens
already used in the rest of the app.

What changed:
- New file: src/bpmn/miro-theme.css (one import, no JSX touched)
- Tasks: blue (User/Task), purple (Service/Script), green (Send/Receive),
  coral (Business rule), gray (Manual), yellow (Call activity),
  white-with-dashed-border (Sub-process)
- Events: green start, yellow intermediate, coral end
- Gateways: yellow XOR, green AND, purple event-based, gray complex
- Pools: light-blue; Lanes: white with blue dividers
- Soft drop-shadow on every shape, rounded palette/popup/context-pad
- Soft 24px grid on the canvas background
- Inter font for labels (system fallback)
- No changes to behavior: selection, hover, snap, autosave, properties
  panel and diff-highlight all still work

Tests: 68/68 pass, npm run build clean.
---
